                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The final game in the Trilogy of \"The Journey Down\". It fulfilled my expectation of being longer with better graphics and more puzzles.\r\n\r\nThere are more locales to explore and you will be back tracking quite frequently to complete the puzzles. Surprisingly, I wasn't bored or frustrated which speaks a lot about the level design and story progression.\r\n\r\nThe story pacing is handled well and the \"Behind the Scenes\" shows there were lot of more locations that were cut out in the final draft. \r\n\r\nIn all, playing all 3 games during a weekend isn't a bad deal.\r\n\r\n- 8/10",
